            "output": "<path>/workspace/apis/python/src/tiledb/vector_search/ivf_flat_index.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"\n2: IVFFlat Index implementation.\n3: \n4: IVFFlatIndex is based on `k-means` clustering and shuffling of the dataset vectors.\n5: \n6: During ingestion, TileDB computes the `k-means` clusters and shuffles the vectors into partitions.\n7: The vectors are stored grouped by partition in a 2D TileDB array allowing for partitions to be read\n8: with minimal I/O overhead.\n9: \n10: To answer a query, the search focuses only on a small number of partitions, based on the query’s proximity\n11: to the `k-means` centroids. This is specified with a parameter called `nprobe` controlling how many partitions\n12: are checked for each query.\n13: \n14: IVFFlatIndex provides a vector search implementation that can trade-off accuracy for performance.\n15: \n16: Queries can be run in multiple modes:\n17: \n18: - Local main memory:\n19:   - Loads the entire index in memory during initialization and uses it to answer queries.\n20: - Local out of core:\n21:   - Avoids loading index data in memory by interleaving I/O and query execution, respecting the\n22:   memory budget defined by the user.\n23: - Distributed execution:\n24:   - Executes the queries using multiple workers in TileDB Cloud.\n25: \"\"\"\n26: import json\n27: import multiprocessing\n28: from typing import Any, Mapping\n29: \n30: import numpy as np\n31: \n32: from tiledb.cloud.dag import Mode\n33: from tiledb.vector_search import index\n34: from tiledb.vector_search.module import *\n35: from tiledb.vector_search.storage_formats import STORAGE_VERSION\n36: from tiledb.vector_search.storage_formats import storage_formats\n37: from tiledb.vector_search.storage_formats import validate_storage_version\n38: from tiledb.vector_search.utils import MAX_FLOAT32\n39: from tiledb.vector_search.utils import MAX_INT32\n40: from tiledb.vector_search.utils import MAX_UINT64\n41: from tiledb.vector_search.utils import add_to_group\n42: \n43: TILE_SIZE_BYTES = 64000000  # 64MB\n44: INDEX_TYPE = \"IVF_FLAT\"\n45: \n46: \n47: def submit_local(d, func, *args, **kwargs):\n48:     # Drop kwarg\n49:     kwargs.pop(\"image_name\", None)\n50:     kwargs.pop(\"resource_class\", None)\n51:     kwargs.pop(\"resources\", None)\n52:     return d.submit_local(func, *args, **kwargs)\n53: \n54: \n55: class IVFFlatIndex(index.Index):\n56:     \"\"\"\n57:     Opens an `IVFFlatIndex`.\n58: \n59:     Parameters\n60:     ----------\n61:     uri: str\n62:         URI of the index.\n63:     config: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]]\n64:         TileDB config dictionary.\n65:     timestamp: int or tuple(int)\n66:         If int, open the index at a given timestamp.\n67:         If tuple, open at the given start and end timestamps.\n68:     memory_budget: int\n69:         Main memory budget, in number of vectors, for query execution.\n70:         If not provided, all index data are loaded in main memory.\n71:         Otherwise, no index data are loaded in main memory and this memory budget is\n72:         applied during queries.\n73:     open_for_remote_query_execution: bool\n74:         If `True`, do not load any index data in main memory locally, and instead load index data in the TileDB Cloud taskgraph created when a non-`None` `driver_mode` is passed to `query()`. We then load index data in the taskgraph based on `memory_budget`.\n75:         If `False`, load index data in main memory locally according to `memory_budget`. Note that you can still use a taskgraph for query execution, you'll just end up loading the data both on your local machine and in the cloud taskgraph..\n76:     \"\"\"\n77: \n78:     def __init__(\n79:         self,\n80:         uri: str,\n81:         config: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,\n82:         timestamp=None,\n83:         memory_budget: int = -1,\n84:         open_for_remote_query_execution: bool = False,\n85:         **kwargs,\n86:     ):\n87:         self.index_open_kwargs = {\n88:             \"uri\": uri,\n89:             \"config\": config,\n90:             \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n91:             \"memory_budget\": memory_budget,\n92:         }\n93:         self.index_open_kwargs.update(kwargs)\n94:         self.index_type = INDEX_TYPE\n95:         super().__init__(\n96:             uri=uri,\n97:             config=config,\n98:             timestamp=timestamp,\n99:             open_for_remote_query_execution=open_for_remote_query_execution,\n100:         )\n101:         self.db_uri = self.group[\n102:             storage_formats[self.storage_version][\"PARTS_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n103:             + self.index_version\n104:         ].uri\n105:         self.centroids_uri = self.group[\n106:             storage_formats[self.storage_version][\"CENTROIDS_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n107:             + self.index_version\n108:         ].uri\n109:         self.index_array_uri = self.group[\n110:             storage_formats[self.storage_version][\"INDEX_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n111:             + self.index_version\n112:         ].uri\n113:         self.ids_uri = self.group[\n114:             storage_formats[self.storage_version][\"IDS_ARRAY_NAME\"] + self.index_version\n115:         ].uri\n116:         self.memory_budget = memory_budget\n117: \n118:         schema = tiledb.ArraySchema.load(self.db_uri, ctx=tiledb.Ctx(self.config))\n119:         self.dimensions = schema.shape[0]\n120: \n121:         self.dtype = self.group.meta.get(\"dtype\", None)\n122:         if self.dtype is None:\n123:             self.dtype = np.dtype(schema.attr(\"values\").dtype)\n124:         else:\n125:             self.dtype = np.dtype(self.dtype)\n126: \n127:         if self.base_size == 0:\n128:             self.size = 0\n129:             self.partitions = 0\n130:             return\n131: \n132:         self.partition_history = [\n133:             int(x)\n134:             for x in list(json.loads(self.group.meta.get(\"partition_history\", \"[]\")))\n135:         ]\n136:         if len(self.partition_history) == 0:\n137:             schema = tiledb.ArraySchema.load(\n138:                 self.centroids_uri, ctx=tiledb.Ctx(self.config)\n139:             )\n140:             self.partitions = schema.domain.dim(\"cols\").domain[1] + 1\n141:         else:\n142:             self.partitions = self.partition_history[self.history_index]\n143: \n144:         if not open_for_remote_query_execution:\n145:             self._centroids = load_as_matrix(\n146:                 self.centroids_uri,\n147:                 ctx=self.ctx,\n148:                 size=self.partitions,\n149:                 config=config,\n150:                 timestamp=self.base_array_timestamp,\n151:             )\n152:             self._index = read_vector_u64(\n153:                 self.ctx,\n154:                 self.index_array_uri,\n155:                 0,\n156:                 self.partitions + 1,\n157:                 self.base_array_timestamp,\n158:             )\n159: \n160:         if self.base_size == -1:\n161:             self.size = self._index[self.partitions]\n162:         else:\n163:             self.size = self.base_size\n164: \n165:         # TODO pass in a context\n166:         if not open_for_remote_query_execution and self.memory_budget == -1:\n167:             self._db = load_as_matrix(\n168:                 self.db_uri,\n169:                 ctx=self.ctx,\n170:                 config=config,\n171:                 size=self.size,\n172:                 timestamp=self.base_array_timestamp,\n173:             )\n174:             self._ids = read_vector_u64(\n175:                 self.ctx, self.ids_uri, 0, self.size, self.base_array_timestamp\n176:             )\n177: \n178:     def get_dimensions(self):\n179:         \"\"\"\n180:         Returns the dimension of the vectors in the index.\n181:         \"\"\"\n182:         return self.dimensions\n183: \n184:     def query_internal(\n185:         self,\n186:         queries: np.ndarray,\n187:         k: int = 10,\n188:         nprobe: int = 1,\n189:         nthreads: int = -1,\n190:         use_nuv_implementation: bool = False,\n191:         mode: Mode = None,\n192:         resource_class: Optional[str] = None,\n193:         resources: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,\n194:         num_partitions: int = -1,\n195:         num_workers: int = -1,\n196:         **kwargs,\n197:     ):\n198:         \"\"\"\n199:         Queries an `IVFFlatIndex`.\n200: \n201:         Parameters\n202:         ----------\n203:         queries: np.ndarray\n204:             2D array of query vectors. This can be used as a batch query interface by passing multiple queries in one call.\n205:         k: int\n206:             Number of results to return per query vector.\n207:         nprobe: int\n208:             Number of partitions to check per query.\n209:             Use this parameter to trade-off accuracy for latency and cost.\n210:         nthreads: int\n211:             Number of threads to use for local query execution.\n212:         use_nuv_implementation: bool\n213:             Whether to use the nuv query implementation. Default: False\n214:         mode: Mode\n215:             If provided the query will be executed using TileDB cloud taskgraphs.\n216:             For distributed execution you can use REALTIME or BATCH mode.\n217:             For local execution you can use LOCAL mode.\n218:         resource_class:\n219:             The name of the resource class to use (\"standard\" or \"large\"). Resource classes define maximum\n220:             limits for cpu and memory usage. Can only be used in REALTIME or BATCH mode.\n221:             Cannot be used alongside resources.\n222:             In REALTIME or BATCH mode if neither resource_class nor resources are provided,\n223:             we default to the \"large\" resource class.\n224:         resources:\n225:             A specification for the amount of resources to use when executing using TileDB cloud\n226:             taskgraphs, of the form: {\"cpu\": \"6\", \"memory\": \"12Gi\", \"gpu\": 1}. Can only be used\n227:             in BATCH mode. Cannot be used alongside resource_class.\n228:         num_partitions: int\n229:             Only relevant for taskgraph based execution.\n230:             If provided, we split the query execution in that many partitions.\n231:         num_workers: int\n232:             Only relevant for taskgraph based execution.\n233:             If provided, this is the number of workers to use for the query execution.\n234:         \"\"\"\n235:         if self.size == 0:\n236:             return np.full((queries.shape[0], k), MAX_FLOAT32), np.full(\n237:                 (queries.shape[0], k), MAX_UINT64\n238:             )\n239: \n240:         if mode != Mode.BATCH and resources:\n241:             raise TypeError(\"Can only pass resources in BATCH mode\")\n242:         if (mode != Mode.REALTIME and mode != Mode.BATCH) and resource_class:\n243:             raise TypeError(\"Can only pass resource_class in REALTIME or BATCH mode\")\n244: \n245:         if queries.ndim == 1:\n246:             queries = np.array([queries])\n247: \n248:         if nthreads == -1:\n249:             nthreads = multiprocessing.cpu_count()\n250: \n251:         nprobe = min(nprobe, self.partitions)\n252:         if mode is None:\n253:             queries_m = array_to_matrix(np.transpose(queries))\n254:             if self.memory_budget == -1:\n255:                 d, i = ivf_query_ram(\n256:                     self.dtype,\n257:                     self._db,\n258:                     self._centroids,\n259:                     queries_m,\n260:                     self._index,\n261:                     self._ids,\n262:                     nprobe=nprobe,\n263:                     k_nn=k,\n264:                     nthreads=nthreads,\n265:                     ctx=self.ctx,\n266:                     use_nuv_implementation=use_nuv_implementation,\n267:                 )\n268:             else:\n269:                 d, i = ivf_query(\n270:                     self.dtype,\n271:                     self.db_uri,\n272:                     self._centroids,\n273:                     queries_m,\n274:                     self._index,\n275:                     self.ids_uri,\n276:                     nprobe=nprobe,\n277:                     k_nn=k,\n278:                     memory_budget=self.memory_budget,\n279:                     nthreads=nthreads,\n280:                     ctx=self.ctx,\n281:                     use_nuv_implementation=use_nuv_implementation,\n282:                     timestamp=self.base_array_timestamp,\n283:                 )\n284: \n285:             return np.transpose(np.array(d)), np.transpose(np.array(i))\n286:         else:\n287:             return self._taskgraph_query(\n288:                 queries=queries,\n289:                 k=k,\n290:                 nthreads=nthreads,\n291:                 nprobe=nprobe,\n292:                 mode=mode,\n293:                 resource_class=resource_class,\n294:                 resources=resources,\n295:                 num_partitions=num_partitions,\n296:                 num_workers=num_workers,\n297:                 config=self.config,\n298:             )\n299: \n300:     def _taskgraph_query(\n301:         self,\n302:         queries: np.ndarray,\n303:         k: int = 10,\n304:         nprobe: int = 10,\n305:         nthreads: int = -1,\n306:         mode: Mode = None,\n307:         resource_class: Optional[str] = None,\n308:         resources: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,\n309:         num_partitions: int = -1,\n310:         num_workers: int = -1,\n311:         config: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,\n312:     ):\n313:         \"\"\"\n314:         Query an IVF_FLAT index using TileDB cloud taskgraphs\n315: \n316:         Parameters\n317:         ----------\n318:         queries: numpy.ndarray\n319:             ND Array of queries\n320:         k: int\n321:             Number of top results to return per query\n322:         nprobe: int\n323:             number of probes\n324:         nthreads: int\n325:             Number of threads to use for query\n326:         mode: Mode\n327:             If provided the query will be executed using TileDB cloud taskgraphs.\n328:             For distributed execution you can use REALTIME or BATCH mode.\n329:             For local execution you can use LOCAL mode.\n330:         resource_class:\n331:             The name of the resource class to use (\"standard\" or \"large\"). Resource classes define maximum\n332:             limits for cpu and memory usage. Can only be used in REALTIME or BATCH mode.\n333:             Cannot be used alongside resources.\n334:             In REALTIME or BATCH mode if neither resource_class nor resources are provided,\n335:             we default to the \"large\" resource class.\n336:         resources:\n337:             A specification for the amount of resources to use when executing using TileDB cloud\n338:             taskgraphs, of the form: {\"cpu\": \"6\", \"memory\": \"12Gi\", \"gpu\": 1}. Can only be used\n339:             in BATCH mode. Cannot be used alongside resource_class.\n340:         num_partitions: int\n341:             Only relevant for taskgraph based execution.\n342:             If provided, we split the query execution in that many partitions.\n343:         num_workers: int\n344:             Only relevant for taskgraph based execution.\n345:             If provided, this is the number of workers to use for the query execution.\n346:         config: None\n347:             config dictionary, defaults to None\n348:         \"\"\"\n349:         import math\n350:         from functools import partial\n351: \n352:         import numpy as np\n353: \n354:         from tiledb.cloud import dag\n355:         from tiledb.cloud.dag import Mode\n356:         from tiledb.vector_search.module import array_to_matrix\n357:         from tiledb.vector_search.module import dist_qv\n358:         from tiledb.vector_search.module import partition_ivf_index\n359: \n360:         if resource_class and resources:\n361:             raise TypeError(\"Cannot provide both resource_class and resources\")\n362: \n363:         def dist_qv_udf(\n364:             dtype: np.dtype,\n365:             parts_uri: str,\n366:             ids_uri: str,\n367:             query_vectors: np.ndarray,\n368:             active_partitions: np.array,\n369:             active_queries: np.array,\n370:             indices: np.array,\n371:             k_nn: int,\n372:             config: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,\n373:             timestamp: int = 0,\n374:             memory_budget: int = -1,\n375:         ):\n376:             queries_m = array_to_matrix(np.transpose(query_vectors))\n377:             r = dist_qv(\n378:                 dtype=dtype,\n379:                 parts_uri=parts_uri,\n380:                 ids_uri=ids_uri,\n381:                 query_vectors=queries_m,\n382:                 active_partitions=active_partitions,\n383:                 active_queries=active_queries,\n384:                 indices=indices,\n385:                 k_nn=k_nn,\n386:                 ctx=Ctx(config),\n387:                 timestamp=timestamp,\n388:                 # TODO(nikos) add this after the library change gets released in TileDB cloud\n389:                 # upper_bound=0 if memory_budget == -1 else memory_budget,\n390:             )\n391:             results = []\n392:             for q in range(len(r)):\n393:                 tmp_results = []\n394:                 for j in range(len(r[q])):\n395:                     tmp_results.append(r[q][j])\n396:                 results.append(tmp_results)\n397:             return results\n398: \n399:         if num_partitions == -1:\n400:             num_partitions = 5\n401:         if num_workers == -1:\n402:             num_workers = num_partitions\n403:         if mode == Mode.BATCH:\n404:             d = dag.DAG(\n405:                 name=\"vector-query\",\n406:                 mode=Mode.BATCH,\n407:                 max_workers=num_workers,\n408:             )\n409:         elif mode == Mode.REALTIME:\n410:             d = dag.DAG(\n411:                 name=\"vector-query\",\n412:                 mode=Mode.REALTIME,\n413:                 max_workers=num_workers,\n414:             )\n415:         else:\n416:             d = dag.DAG(\n417:                 name=\"vector-query\",\n418:                 mode=Mode.REALTIME,\n419:                 max_workers=1,\n420:                 namespace=\"default\",\n421:             )\n422:         submit = partial(submit_local, d)\n423:         if mode == Mode.BATCH or mode == Mode.REALTIME:\n424:             submit = d.submit\n425: \n426:         queries_m = array_to_matrix(np.transpose(queries))\n427:         active_partitions, active_queries = partition_ivf_index(\n428:             centroids=self._centroids, query=queries_m, nprobe=nprobe, nthreads=nthreads\n429:         )\n430:         num_parts = len(active_partitions)\n431: \n432:         parts_per_node = int(math.ceil(num_parts / num_partitions))\n433:         nodes = []\n434:         for part in range(0, num_parts, parts_per_node):\n435:             part_end = part + parts_per_node\n436:             if part_end > num_parts:\n437:                 part_end = num_parts\n438:             aq = []\n439:             for tt in range(part, part_end):\n440:                 aqt = []\n441:                 for ttt in range(len(active_queries[tt])):\n442:                     aqt.append(active_queries[tt][ttt])\n443:                 aq.append(aqt)\n444:             nodes.append(\n445:                 submit(\n446:                     dist_qv_udf,\n447:                     dtype=self.dtype,\n448:                     parts_uri=self.db_uri,\n449:                     ids_uri=self.ids_uri,\n450:                     query_vectors=queries,\n451:                     active_partitions=np.array(active_partitions)[part:part_end],\n452:                     active_queries=np.array(aq, dtype=object),\n453:                     indices=np.array(self._index),\n454:                     k_nn=k,\n455:                     config=config,\n456:                     timestamp=self.base_array_timestamp,\n457:                     memory_budget=self.memory_budget,\n458:                     resource_class=\"large\"\n459:                     if (not resources and not resource_class)\n460:                     else resource_class,\n461:                     resources=resources,\n462:                     image_name=\"3.9-vectorsearch\",\n463:                 )\n464:             )\n465: \n466:         d.compute()\n467:         d.wait()\n468:         results = []\n469:         for node in nodes:\n470:             res = node.result()\n471:             results.append(res)\n472: \n473:         results_per_query_d = []\n474:         results_per_query_i = []\n475:         for q in range(queries.shape[0]):\n476:             tmp_results = []\n477:             for j in range(k):\n478:                 for r in results:\n479:                     if len(r[q]) > j:\n480:                         if r[q][j][0] > 0:\n481:                             tmp_results.append(r[q][j])\n482:             tmp = sorted(tmp_results, key=lambda t: t[0])[0:k]\n483:             for j in range(len(tmp), k):\n484:                 tmp.append((float(0.0), int(0)))\n485:             results_per_query_d.append(np.array(tmp, dtype=np.float32)[:, 0])\n486:             results_per_query_i.append(np.array(tmp, dtype=np.uint64)[:, 1])\n487:         return np.array(results_per_query_d), np.array(results_per_query_i)\n488: \n489: \n490: def create(\n491:     uri: str,\n492:     dimensions: int,\n493:     vector_type: np.dtype,\n494:     group_exists: bool = False,\n495:     config: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]] = None,\n496:     storage_version: str = STORAGE_VERSION,\n497:     distance_metric: vspy.DistanceMetric = vspy.DistanceMetric.L2,\n498:     **kwargs,\n499: ) -> IVFFlatIndex:\n500:     \"\"\"\n501:     Creates an empty IVFFlatIndex.\n502: \n503:     Parameters\n504:     ----------\n505:     uri: str\n506:         URI of the index.\n507:     dimensions: int\n508:         Number of dimensions for the vectors to be stored in the index.\n509:     vector_type: np.dtype\n510:         Datatype of vectors.\n511:         Supported values (uint8, int8, float32).\n512:     group_exists: bool\n513:         If False it creates the TileDB group for the index.\n514:         If True the method expects the TileDB group to be already created.\n515:     config: Optional[Mapping[str, Any]]\n516:         TileDB config dictionary.\n517:     storage_version: str\n518:         The TileDB vector search storage version to use.\n519:         If not provided, use the latest stable storage version.\n520:     \"\"\"\n521:     validate_storage_version(storage_version)\n522: \n523:     if distance_metric != vspy.DistanceMetric.L2:\n524:         raise ValueError(\n525:             f\"Distance metric {distance_metric} is not supported in IVF_FLAT\"\n526:         )\n527: \n528:     index.create_metadata(\n529:         uri=uri,\n530:         dimensions=dimensions,\n531:         vector_type=vector_type,\n532:         index_type=INDEX_TYPE,\n533:         storage_version=storage_version,\n534:         distance_metric=distance_metric,\n535:         group_exists=group_exists,\n536:         config=config,\n537:     )\n538:     with tiledb.scope_ctx(ctx_or_config=config):\n539:         group = tiledb.Group(uri, \"w\")\n540:         tile_size = int(TILE_SIZE_BYTES / np.dtype(vector_type).itemsize / dimensions)\n541:         group.meta[\"partition_history\"] = json.dumps([0])\n542:         centroids_array_name = storage_formats[storage_version][\"CENTROIDS_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n543:         index_array_name = storage_formats[storage_version][\"INDEX_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n544:         ids_array_name = storage_formats[storage_version][\"IDS_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n545:         parts_array_name = storage_formats[storage_version][\"PARTS_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n546:         updates_array_name = storage_formats[storage_version][\"UPDATES_ARRAY_NAME\"]\n547:         centroids_uri = f\"{uri}/{centroids_array_name}\"\n548:         index_array_uri = f\"{uri}/{index_array_name}\"\n549:         ids_uri = f\"{uri}/{ids_array_name}\"\n550:         parts_uri = f\"{uri}/{parts_array_name}\"\n551:         updates_array_uri = f\"{uri}/{updates_array_name}\"\n552: \n553:         centroids_array_rows_dim = tiledb.Dim(\n554:             name=\"rows\",\n555:             domain=(0, dimensions - 1),\n556:             tile=dimensions,\n557:             dtype=np.dtype(np.int32),\n558:         )\n559:         centroids_array_cols_dim = tiledb.Dim(\n560:             name=\"cols\",\n561:             domain=(0, MAX_INT32),\n562:             tile=100000,\n563:             dtype=np.dtype(np.int32),\n564:         )\n565:         centroids_array_dom = tiledb.Domain(\n566:             centroids_array_rows_dim, centroids_array_cols_dim\n567:         )\n568:         centroids_attr = tiledb.Attr(\n569:             name=\"centroids\",\n570:             dtype=np.dtype(np.float32),\n571:             filters=storage_formats[storage_version][\"DEFAULT_ATTR_FILTERS\"],\n572:         )\n573:         centroids_schema = tiledb.ArraySchema(\n574:             domain=centroids_array_dom,\n575:             sparse=False,\n576:             attrs=[centroids_attr],\n577:             cell_order=\"col-major\",\n578:             tile_order=\"col-major\",\n579:         )\n580:         tiledb.Array.create(centroids_uri, centroids_schema)\n581:         add_to_group(group, centroids_uri, name=centroids_array_name)\n582: \n583:         index_array_rows_dim = tiledb.Dim(\n584:             name=\"rows\",\n585:             domain=(0, MAX_INT32),\n586:             tile=100000,\n587:             dtype=np.dtype(np.int32),\n588:         )\n589:         index_array_dom = tiledb.Domain(index_array_rows_dim)\n590:         index_attr = tiledb.Attr(\n591:             name=\"values\",\n592:             dtype=np.dtype(np.uint64),\n593:             filters=storage_formats[storage_version][\"DEFAULT_ATTR_FILTERS\"],\n594:         )\n595:         index_schema = tiledb.ArraySchema(\n596:             domain=index_array_dom,\n597:             sparse=False,\n598:             attrs=[index_attr],\n599:             cell_order=\"col-major\",\n600:             tile_order=\"col-major\",\n601:         )\n602:         tiledb.Array.create(index_array_uri, index_schema)\n603:         add_to_group(group, index_array_uri, name=index_array_name)\n604: \n605:         ids_array_rows_dim = tiledb.Dim(\n606:             name=\"rows\",\n607:             domain=(0, MAX_INT32),\n608:             tile=tile_size,\n609:             dtype=np.dtype(np.int32),\n610:         )\n611:         ids_array_dom = tiledb.Domain(ids_array_rows_dim)\n612:         ids_attr = tiledb.Attr(\n613:             name=\"values\",\n614:             dtype=np.dtype(np.uint64),\n615:             filters=storage_formats[storage_version][\"DEFAULT_ATTR_FILTERS\"],\n616:         )\n617:         ids_schema = tiledb.ArraySchema(\n618:             domain=ids_array_dom,\n619:             sparse=False,\n620:             attrs=[ids_attr],\n621:             cell_order=\"col-major\",\n622:             tile_order=\"col-major\",\n623:         )\n624:         tiledb.Array.create(ids_uri, ids_schema)\n625:         add_to_group(group, ids_uri, name=ids_array_name)\n626: \n627:         parts_array_rows_dim = tiledb.Dim(\n628:             name=\"rows\",\n629:             domain=(0, dimensions - 1),\n630:             tile=dimensions,\n631:             dtype=np.dtype(np.int32),\n632:         )\n633:         parts_array_cols_dim = tiledb.Dim(\n634:             name=\"cols\",\n635:             domain=(0, MAX_INT32),\n636:             tile=tile_size,\n637:             dtype=np.dtype(np.int32),\n638:         )\n639:         parts_array_dom = tiledb.Domain(parts_array_rows_dim, parts_array_cols_dim)\n640:         parts_attr = tiledb.Attr(\n641:             name=\"values\",\n642:             dtype=vector_type,\n643:             filters=storage_formats[storage_version][\"DEFAULT_ATTR_FILTERS\"],\n644:         )\n645:         parts_schema = tiledb.ArraySchema(\n646:             domain=parts_array_dom,\n647:             sparse=False,\n648:             attrs=[parts_attr],\n649:             cell_order=\"col-major\",\n650:             tile_order=\"col-major\",\n651:         )\n652:         tiledb.Array.create(parts_uri, parts_schema)\n653:         add_to_group(group, parts_uri, name=parts_array_name)\n654: \n655:         external_id_dim = tiledb.Dim(\n656:             name=\"external_id\",\n657:             domain=(0, MAX_UINT64 - 1),\n658:             dtype=np.dtype(np.uint64),\n659:         )\n660:         dom = tiledb.Domain(external_id_dim)\n661:         vector_attr = tiledb.Attr(name=\"vector\", dtype=vector_type, var=True)\n662:         updates_schema = tiledb.ArraySchema(\n663:             domain=dom,\n664:             sparse=True,\n665:             attrs=[vector_attr],\n666:             allows_duplicates=False,\n667:         )\n668:         tiledb.Array.create(updates_array_uri, updates_schema)\n669:         add_to_group(group, updates_array_uri, name=updates_array_name)\n670: \n671:         group.close()\n672:         return IVFFlatIndex(uri=uri, config=config, memory_budget=1000000)\n\n(End of file - total 672 lines)\n</content>",
            "metadata": {
              "preview": "\"\"\"\nIVFFlat Index implementation.\n\nIVFFlatIndex is based on `k-means` clustering and shuffling of the dataset vectors.\n\nDuring ingestion, TileDB computes the `k-means` clusters and shuffles the vectors into partitions.\nThe vectors are stored grouped by partition in a 2D TileDB array allowing for partitions to be read\nwith minimal I/O overhead.\n\nTo answer a query, the search focuses only on a small number of partitions, based on the query’s proximity\nto the `k-means` centroids. This is specified with a parameter called `nprobe` controlling how many partitions\nare checked for each query.\n\nIVFFlatIndex provides a vector search implementation that can trade-off accuracy for performance.\n\nQueries can be run in multiple modes:\n\n- Local main memory:\n  - Loads the entire index in memory during initialization and uses it to answer queries.\n- Local out of core:",
